.TH "HOMELAB-WAKE" "1" "2026-11-06" "Homelab ops"
.SH NAME
homelab-wake \- Send Wake-on-LAN packets directly or through an awake relay.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homelab-wake
[arguments]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send Wake-on-LAN packets directly or through an awake relay.
Established names and consumer paths are preserved. No hardware or service action was executed for documentation verification.
.SH INTERFACE
.SS /usr/local/bin/homelab-wake
Source: shared/scripts/wake
.nf
parser.add_argument('target',nargs='?',choices=['nexus','tensor','qubit','both'])
parser.add_argument('--via',choices=['nexus','tensor'],help='Send from this awake relay over SSH/Tailscale')
parser.add_argument('--source',help='Local IPv4 address to bind for direct LAN sending')
parser.add_argument('--list',action='store_true',help='Show recorded hosts; send nothing')
parser.add_argument('--config',type=pathlib.Path)
.fi

.SH DEPENDENCIES
Use the interpreter in the source shebang and the existing host packages and services referenced in that source. Host configuration and private credentials remain on their original host.
.SH OPERATIONS
Before changing behavior, inspect inventory/audit-2026-11-06/nexus.json for recorded consumers and the source above for exact dependency paths. Never invoke a power, desktop, network, credential, notification, or storage operation merely to test it.
.SH SOURCE
Private iragonforce/ops repository. Consult docs/workflow.md for deployment, verification, rollback, and change records.
